#version 450
#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : require
// AMEVA TIMESTEP_EMBEDDING (ggml_compute_forward_timestep_embedding_f32): for timestep t_i and j < half = dim / 2,
//   dst[i][j] = cos(t_i * freq[j]), dst[i][half + j] = sin(t_i * freq[j]), freq[j] = exp(-log(max_period) * j / half)
// and, for an odd dim, dst[i][dim - 1] = 0.
//
// freq comes from the host as a table computed with ggml's expression (the argument t * freq[j] is then the CPU's,
// bit for bit: a frequency that differs by a few ulp would move the argument by 1e-3 at t = 1000). Sine and cosine
// are computed here and not with the built-in functions, whose error bound in Vulkan is absolute 2^-11 and holds
// inside [-pi, pi] only, while the arguments reach max timestep (1000): the argument is reduced by multiples of pi / 4
// held in three parts (the products with the first two are exact for |x| < 8192) and the remainder goes through
// polynomials of degree 7 (sine) and 8 (cosine), the single-precision routines of the Cephes library. Every step is
// rounded on its own (precise). Against the CPU's libm the results differ in the last bits (tests/ameva_unet_ops_check
// measures it); above |x| = 8192 the reduction loses accuracy gradually.
//
//   binding 0: timesteps f32 (contiguous), binding 1: dst f32 [dim, n], binding 2: freq f32 [half]
//   push: dim, half, n, a_off, d_off, d_s1 (floats), f_off
//   grid: one invocation per element of dst, 1-D index space (ameva_linear_id)
layout(local_size_x = 64, local_size_y = 1, local_size_z = 1) in;

#include "ameva_common.glsl"

layout(std430, binding = 0) readonly buffer A { float ts[]; };
layout(std430, binding = 1) writeonly buffer D { float dst[]; };
layout(std430, binding = 2) readonly buffer F { float freq[]; };

layout(push_constant) uniform PushConstants {
    uint dim, half_dim, n, a_off;
    uint d_off, d_s1, f_off;
} pc;

// sin(x) for want_cos == false, cos(x) otherwise
float sincos(float xx, bool want_cos) {
    precise float x = abs(xx);
    uint j = uint(x * 1.27323954473516); // octant: x / (pi / 4)
    precise float y = float(j);
    if ((j & 1u) != 0u) {
        j += 1u;
        y += 1.0;
    }
    j &= 7u;
    bool neg = !want_cos && xx < 0.0;
    if (j > 3u) {
        neg = !neg;
        j -= 4u;
    }
    if (want_cos && j > 1u) neg = !neg;
    // x - y * pi / 4 in three steps
    x = x - y * 0.78515625;
    x = x - y * 2.4187564849853515625e-4;
    x = x - y * 3.77489497744594108e-8;
    precise float z = x * x;
    precise float r;
    if ((j == 1u || j == 2u) != want_cos) {
        r = 2.443315711809948e-5;
        r = r * z - 1.388731625493765e-3;
        r = r * z + 4.166664568298827e-2;
        r = r * (z * z);
        r = r - 0.5 * z;
        r = r + 1.0;
    } else {
        r = -1.9515295891e-4;
        r = r * z + 8.3321608736e-3;
        r = r * z - 1.6666654611e-1;
        r = r * (z * x);
        r = r + x;
    }
    return neg ? -r : r;
}

void main() {
    const uint k = ameva_linear_id();
    if (k >= pc.n * pc.dim) return;
    const uint i = k / pc.dim, j = k - i * pc.dim;
    float r = 0.0; // the last element of an odd dim
    if (j < 2u * pc.half_dim) {
        const bool want_cos = j < pc.half_dim;
        precise float arg = ts[pc.a_off + i] * freq[pc.f_off + (want_cos ? j : j - pc.half_dim)];
        r = sincos(arg, want_cos);
    }
    dst[pc.d_off + i * pc.d_s1 + j] = r;
}
